[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Blessing in Disguise?]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.01]Why does the vicar refuse to cut down the tree? | 为什么牧师拒绝砍掉那棵树？
[00:16.94]The tiny village of Frinley is said to possess a 'cursed tree'. | 据说弗林利这个小村里有一棵“被诅咒的树”。
[00:22.89]Because the tree was mentioned in a newspaper, | 就因为报纸上报道过这棵树，
[00:26.47]the number of visitors to Frinley has now increased. | 现在到弗林利来参观的人越来越多。
[00:31.71]The tree was planted near the church fifty years ago, but it is only in recent years that it has gained an evil reputation. | 这棵树是50年前栽在教堂附近的，但只是近几年才得了一个坏名声。
[00:43.07]It is said that if anyone touches the tree, he will have bad luck; if he picks a leaf, he will die. | 据说谁碰了这棵树谁就会倒霉，如果摘一片树叶，就会死。
[00:52.89]Many villagers believe that the tree has already claimed a number of victims. | 很多村民相信这棵树已害了不少人。
[00:59.95]The vicar has been asked to have the tree cut down, but so far he has refused. | 人们曾请求牧师把树砍掉，但直到现在他都没有答应。
[01:08.52]He has pointed out that the tree is a useful source of income, | 他指出这棵树是一个有利可图的财源，
[01:14.13]as tourists have been coming from all parts of the country to see it. | 因为游客们一直从全国各地纷纷前来参观。
[01:20.04]In spite of all that has been said, | 尽管众说纷纭，
[01:23.23]the tourists have been picking leaves and cutting their names on the tree-trunk. | 游客们还是照常摘树叶，把名字刻在树干上。
[01:29.10]So far, not one of them has been struck down by sudden death! | 到目前为止，还没有一个人突然死去呢！
